---
/**
 * WritingThumb.astro — CSS-only thumbnail abstract for writing-type works.
 *
 * Why: Phase 1 ships no per-item imagery (ADR 0010); thumbs are uniform-aspect
 * CSS abstractions to maintain visual rhythm without LCP risk.
 * Three horizontal lines of varying widths mimic a text excerpt, giving an
 * immediately legible "document" metaphor without any imagery.
 *
 * @see packages/specs/adrs/0010-cards-no-image-pipeline-yet.md
 */
---

<div class="thumb" aria-hidden="true">
	<div class="lines">
		<div class="line line-a"></div>
		<div class="line line-b"></div>
		<div class="line line-c"></div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.thumb {
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 5%, transparent);
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
		color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 60%, transparent);
	}

	.lines {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		width: 6rem;
	}

	.line {
		height: 0.3125rem;
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
		background: currentColor;
	}

	.line-a {
		width: 100%;
	}
	.line-b {
		width: 85%;
	}
	.line-c {
		width: 65%;
	}
</style>
